From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meenmachine1 <78238681+meenmachine1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:34:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Decompiler: leave a LOAD or STORE whose constant address
 range would wrap

- Fails: "Trying to construct memory range beyond end of address space:
  ram" (LowlevelError from AddrSpaceManager::constructWrappingAddress, via
  Funcdata::newVarnodeOut / newVarnode), and the whole function fails to
  decompile.
- Cause: RuleLoadVarnode and RuleStoreVarnode turn a LOAD or STORE through
  a constant pointer into a COPY from or to a varnode at that address. When
  the address is within size bytes of the end of a space that doesn't allow
  wrapped ranges (ram), that varnode can't exist. The constant typically
  comes from folding a read-only pointer slot whose bytes are 0xffffffff
  (erased flash in firmware), so storing through it addresses the top of
  memory.
- Patch: in both rules, keep the LOAD or STORE (return 0) when the range
  isn't valid in a heritaged space that doesn't allow wrapping: exactly the
  case where newVarnode(Out) would throw. Nothing else changes; the
  function decompiles with the access through the pointer (*(uint *)
  0xffffffff = v).
- Seen on: ARM (v4t) firmware loaded raw with its image read-only;
  reproduced with a synthetic image (a read-only slot holding 0xffffffff,
  stored through).
- Ghidra 12.1.4: the Java decompiler interface reports the same error.

diff --git a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/ruleaction.cc b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/ruleaction.cc
index 3071e76..aa1acff 100644
--- a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/ruleaction.cc
+++ b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/ruleaction.cc
@@ -4305,6 +4305,8 @@ int4 RuleLoadVarnode::applyOp(PcodeOp *op,Funcdata &data)
 
   size = op->getOut()->getSize();
   offoff = AddrSpace::addressToByte(offoff,baseoff->getWordSize());
+  if (!Address(baseoff,offoff).isValidRange(size) && baseoff->isHeritaged() && !baseoff->allowsWrappedRange())
+    return 0;			// Range would run past the end of the space: leave the LOAD
   newvn = data.newVarnode(size,baseoff,offoff);
   data.opSetInput(op,newvn,0);
   data.opRemoveInput(op,1);
@@ -4347,6 +4349,8 @@ int4 RuleStoreVarnode::applyOp(PcodeOp *op,Funcdata &data)
   size = op->getIn(2)->getSize();
   offoff = AddrSpace::addressToByte(offoff,baseoff->getWordSize());
   Address addr(baseoff,offoff);
+  if (!addr.isValidRange(size) && baseoff->isHeritaged() && !baseoff->allowsWrappedRange())
+    return 0;			// Range would run past the end of the space: leave the STORE
   data.newVarnodeOut(size, addr,op);
   op->getOut()->setStackStore();	// Mark as originally coming from CPUI_STORE
   data.opRemoveInput(op,1);
